      "{**18 NY3d at 390} OPINION OF THE COURT",
      "The jury convicted defendant on one count of first-degree murder and one count of second-degree murder. Supreme Court{**18 NY3d at 396} sentenced defendant to concurrent sentences of life imprisonment without parole and 25 years to life. The Appellate Division unanimously modified the judgment of conviction and sentence to the extent of vacating the DNA databank fee imposed by Supreme Court and, as so modified, affirmed (, 72 AD3d 544, 545 [1st Dept 2010]). A Judge of this Court granted defendant leave to appeal (15 NY3d 920 [2010]) and we now affirm. "
